From: Daniel Illescas Romero <illescas.daniel@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:15:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/65] P2: AI soldiers move like the player - cod_aiSpeedMode
 (2.4)

User request: "what if soldiers could walk and run too as me?"

- game/ai_cast.h: AICast_CodApplySpeedMode(cast_state_t *cs, int aiCharacter)
  prototype.
- game/ai_cast_think.c: AICast_CodIsHumanType() (SOLDIER/AMERICAN/ELITEGUARD/
  BLACKGUARD/VENOM/PARTISAN/CIVILIAN/FROGMAN/STIMSOLDIER1-3 only -- never
  zombies, lopers, super/proto soldiers, Helga or Heinrich) and
  AICast_CodApplySpeedMode(), called right after the per-think
  WALKING_SPEED/RUNNING_SPEED/CROUCHING_SPEED are re-read from the current
  anim (~L652): mode 1 (default) matches the player's cod_runSpeed/
  walkScale/crouchScale; mode 2 scales the anim-derived values by
  cod_aiSpeedScale; mode 0 is vanilla.
- game/ai_cast_characters.c: same call at spawn time (AICast_CheckLevelAttributes-
  adjacent crouch-speed-scale setup, ~L1464) so AI never run a frame of
  un-matched starting speeds.

Server-only (ai_*.c), never touches bg_pmove.c or AI behaviour/navigation, so
cod_aiSpeedMode 0 is a true vanilla A/B and this is the one deliberate AI
change in the mod (architecture.md section 3).

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
 SP/code/game/ai_cast.h            |  1 +
 SP/code/game/ai_cast_characters.c |  4 ++
 SP/code/game/ai_cast_think.c      | 64 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 69 insertions(+)

